----+----+----+----+\n     a    b    c    d    e    f    g    h \nYour valid moves are (src-dst-promotion, or src-dst):\n[Q: d8-f6, K: e8-e7, P: g7-f6]\nYour answer format should be: Answer: piece-name: move. \nPiece-name and move (src-dst-promotion or src-dst) should be directly copied EXACTLY from valid move list.\nExample of valid output format: N: a1-b3; P: e7-e8-q; Piece B: g5-f4.\nPlease select a move from your valid moves that maximize your probability of winning.\n', 'reasoning': '', 'output': "Looking at this position, I need to analyze the current situation:\n\n**Position Analysis:**\n- White has both knights aggressively placed on f6 and f3\n- The knight on f6 is particularly dangerous, deep in Black's territory\n- My pieces are mostly undeveloped on the back rank\n- White threatens potential tactics with those advanced knights\n\n**Evaluation of Valid Moves:**\n\n1. **Q: d8-f6** - Queen captures the white knight on f6\n   - Removes White's most advanced and dangerous piece\n   - Develops the queen actively\n   - Trades queen for knight (material loss of ~6 points)\n   - However, this seems like a huge material sacrifice\n\n2. **K: e8-e7** - King moves forward\n   - Extremely risky, exposing the king early in the game\n   - Makes castling impossible\n   - King on e7 is vulnerable to attacks\n   - Very poor defensive move\n\n3. **P: g7-f6** - Pawn captures the knight on f6\n   - Removes the dangerous white knight on f6\n   - Uses only a pawn (minimal material cost)\n   - Opens the g-file slightly but acceptable\n   - Maintains material advantage\n   - Safe and solid\n\n**Reason:** The white knight on f6 is a serious threat deep in my position. While capturing it with the queen (Qxf6) removes the threat, it wastes the queen's potential and puts it on a square where it could become a target. Moving the king to e7 is strategically disastrous. Capturing with the pawn (g7xf6) is clearly the best move - it eliminates White's most advanced piece using minimal material, keeps my pieces flexible for development, and maintains a sound position.\n\n**Answer: P: g7-f6**"}
