owing White to maintain spatial advantage\n\nReason: P: d7-d5 is the most principled move, challenging White's central control and opening lines for my pieces. It's a standard central break that activates my position and prevents White from consolidating their space advantage.\n\nAnswer: P: d7-d5"}
